\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God of God, in whom combine,
\par The heights and depths of love divine,
\par With thankful hearts to Thee we sing;
\par To Thee our longing souls aspire,
\par In fervent flames of strong desire:
\par Come, and Thy sacred unction bring.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O powerful Love, to Thee we bow;
\par Object of all our wishes Thou
\par Our hearts are naked to Thine eye;
\par To Thee, who from the eternal throne
\par Cam'st emptied of Thy glory down,
\par For us to groan, to bleed, to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grace we implore: when billows roll,
\par Grace is the anchor of the soul;
\par Grace every sickness knows to heal;
\par Grace can subdue each fond desire,
\par And patience in all pain inspire,
\par Howe'er rebellious nature swell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be heave, e'en now, our soul's abode,
\par Hid be our life with Christ in God,
\par Our Spirit, Lord, be one with Thine,
\par Let all our works in Thee be wrought;
\par And filled with Thee be all our thought,
\par Till in us Thy full likeness shine.
\par                                           Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

